#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523992 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068721 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "bdded031-fd95-5a7f-92d4-c0d6713ba64d" :knowledge-point/title "Calculating the Distance Between Two Points"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5c855929-b300-53bb-b2f5-24705e47b13c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523443} {:answer/id #uuid "6221fb69-119d-504d-b579-13f039a770b9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{65}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523452} {:answer/id #uuid "7c2e9f91-d463-5286-9ed4-c97a3b93b2bc" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "15" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523513} {:answer/id #uuid "c60b17ee-f26e-5eec-9f8d-f02e776c1ea8" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523671} {:answer/id #uuid "ebbeab2f-2e72-502f-8588-62b91c0340f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523747}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ebbeab2f-2e72-502f-8588-62b91c0340f5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "25" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523747} :answer-field/id #uuid "8db667e4-c6ff-50ef-bf4d-33616aab5cf2" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523862}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9dd278e6-83f6-5c4b-b1f1-6a6ae9e2e467" :question/math-academy-id "q-119011" :question/problem "What is the distance between the points $(-4\\sqrt{5},-2\\sqrt{5})$ and $(\\sqrt{5},-12\\sqrt{5})?$" :question/worked-solution "In this case, we have ${{(-4\\sqrt{5},-2\\sqrt{5})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(\\sqrt{5},-12\\sqrt{5})}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})}.$\nSo, the distance $d$ can be calculated using the distance formula, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}d & =\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{(\\sqrt{5}-(-4\\sqrt{5}))}^{2}+{(-12\\sqrt{5}-(-2\\sqrt{5}))}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(5\\sqrt{5})^{2}+(-10\\sqrt{5})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{25(5)+100(5)} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{125+500} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{625} \\\\  & =25\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186523930 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5df52cb5-75b1-58d9-8535-07c1bb87be34" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Length of a Segment"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a941df4e-944d-5b40-96d0-15089e219a36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523612}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a941df4e-944d-5b40-96d0-15089e219a36" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4\\sqrt{2}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523612} :answer-field/id #uuid "69167d57-152a-5b5e-a04c-0fa20c63b0b4" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186523842}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "10bae273-6993-5b75-9a9e-139dcefc8633" :question/math-academy-id "q-216294" :question/problem "![](images/94/941efa39e90b946e68ea9ccc65ab7b97f4fce84d1cccbaa19135f8c87383a22f.png)\n\nThe exact length of $\\overset{―}{AB}$ is{{field-1}}." :question/worked-solution "From the figure, we note that the points $A$ and $B$ have coordinates ${{(-2,3)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(2,7)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})},$ respectively.\n\nTo find the length of $\\overset{―}{AB},$ we use the distance formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AB & =\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2-(-2))^{2}+(7-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{{4}^{2}+{4}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{16+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{32} \\\\  & =4\\sqrt{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186069301 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186068720 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "5df52cb5-75b1-58d9-8535-07c1bb87be34" :knowledge-point/title "Determining the Length of a Segment"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "88eabd55-766f-573b-8305-9db9fb46fea2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "3" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066977} {:answer/id #uuid "b827aac1-596d-54de-9317-02f420f5b264" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066978} {:answer/id #uuid "dc9efbb1-7d26-572a-8d2c-c509a6d4a218" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5\\sqrt{13}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066979} {:answer/id #uuid "f4a39913-c29c-5674-8ad9-5afeccfbe7b7" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "8\\sqrt{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066980} {:answer/id #uuid "4e1c13fe-164d-597b-9a55-f85afdd238b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{65}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066981}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "4e1c13fe-164d-597b-9a55-f85afdd238b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\sqrt{65}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066981} :answer-field/id #uuid "3f04668a-3df1-560e-950f-53985118bf87" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186066976}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "94652e83-5bd0-5884-9087-2e26389b0cf2" :question/math-academy-id "q-3717" :question/problem "![](images/cd/cd878559d6be37faa60bdb33cbebe2f124d09744aa4df7dae40372499116f239.png)\n\nWhat is the length of $\\overset{―}{CD}?$" :question/worked-solution "From the figure, we note that the points $C$ and $D$ have coordinates ${{(-5,3)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{1}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{1})}$ and ${{(2,-1)}_{⏟}}_{\\text{(}{x}_{2}\\text{,}\\,{y}_{2})},$ respectively.\n\nTo find the length of $\\overset{―}{CD},$ we use the distance formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}CD & =\\sqrt{({x}_{2}-{x}_{1})^{2}+({y}_{2}-{y}_{1})^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(2-(-5))^{2}+(-1-3)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{(7)^{2}+(-4)^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{49+16} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{65}\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
